Subject: folder view: back the desktop labels under a light colour scheme

A root-view label is drawn white with a black shadow whatever the colour
scheme. When the window colour set is light (background HSL lightness
above 0.5), draw a rounded black backing at 0.6 opacity behind the
label's painted text, so the white label holds at least 4.5:1 on a light
wallpaper. Under a dark scheme the label is unchanged.
---
--- a/containments/desktop/package/contents/ui/FolderItemDelegate.qml
+++ b/containments/desktop/package/contents/ui/FolderItemDelegate.qml
@@ -305,6 +305,32 @@
                     source: main.decoration
                 }
 
+                Rectangle {
+                    id: labelBacking
+
+                    // A root-view label is white whatever the scheme. Under a light window colour set
+                    // the wallpaper is light too, and the shadow alone leaves the fill at about 1:1
+                    // on it; the backing holds the white text above 4.5:1 on any wallpaper.
+                    Kirigami.Theme.colorSet: Kirigami.Theme.Window
+                    Kirigami.Theme.inherit: false
+
+                    readonly property real paintedWidth: Math.min(label.paintedWidth, label.width)
+
+                    z: 1
+                    visible: main.isOnRootView && label.visible && label.text.length > 0
+                             && Kirigami.Theme.backgroundColor.hslLightness > 0.5
+
+                    x: label.x - Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing
+                       + (label.horizontalAlignment === Text.AlignHCenter ? (label.width - paintedWidth) / 2 : 0)
+                    y: label.y + (label.height - label.paintedHeight) / 2 - Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing / 2
+                    width: paintedWidth + Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing * 2
+                    height: label.paintedHeight + Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing
+
+                    radius: Kirigami.Units.cornerRadius
+                    color: "black"
+                    opacity: 0.6
+                }
+
                 PlasmaExtras.ShadowedLabel {
                     id: label
 
